text.section:
The Board may issue a license to perform residential building energy analysis in the Commonwealth to any applicant who has submitted satisfactory evidence that he has successfully:

Completed an accredited residential building energy analyst training program;


Completed at least five residential building energy analyses under the supervision of a licensed residential building energy analyst;


Remains in good standing with any certifying organization approved by the Board, provided that the requirements for the applicant's class of membership in such association are equal to or exceed the requirements established by the Board for all applicants;


Maintains the necessary insurance coverage as determined by the Board; and


Demonstrates the financial capability, as determined by the Board, to perform residential building energy analysis.
